#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compare the new discovery stage with the existing front end over the corpus.

For every tracked `.brp` file under `blorp/src`, `standard_library/src` and
`blorp/test`, both front ends lex and parse the file, and this script checks
per file that they agree on

  * every token: byte range, kind and text (the existing lexer's `#` followed
    by a name is one `DimensionNameToken` in the new lexer, so that pair is
    merged before comparing),
  * whether the lexer reported a diagnostic, and
  * whether the parser rejected the file (the accept/reject verdict), and,
    for a file both reject, the first diagnostic: its `line:column` must be
    the same, and its message and help must be the same except where a
    `WORDING_DIFFERENCES` or `HELP_DIFFERENCES` entry names the difference
    and its reason.

Each side is one dumper program, compiled to a binary once and run once,
sequentially, over the whole file list:

  * `blorp/test/test_compiler/tools/legacy_front_end_dump.brp` (existing compiler),
  * `blorp/test/test_compiler_new/tools/corpus_dump.brp` (discovery stage).

It also runs the legacy adapter's differential
(`discovery_adapter_differential.brp`): for the same two roots, and once over
every corpus file as a root of one discovery, each module's parsed program
rebuilt from the discovery stage's tables by `discovery_adapter.brp` (every
declaration and every body) must equal the existing parser's with its
interpolation holes parsed, field for field and span for span. A deliberate
difference needs an `ADAPTER_DIFFERENCES` entry naming it and its reason.
The same runs assemble each accepted module on the typed-tree path
(`tree_module_assembly.brp`): every module it reads in full must pass the id
census and its whole projected program must equal the existing parser's; the
others are counted by where the tree path stopped reading them.

It also checks the discovery stage's module graph (`discovery_module_order_dump.brp`)
for one compile root and one `blorp test` root: it must load at least the
expected number of modules, so a root or package that failed to resolve cannot
pass, and a package fixture must contribute a module with its origin. The same
roots run again with the standard library read from the compiler's embedded
texts (no standard-library directory), and a fixture project runs with two
`blorp.toml` source packages (an export, a module that is not exported, an
internal import and a relative import that must stay in its package).

A mismatch is printed with its file and, for tokens, the first differing
token. Exit status 0 means every file agrees.

With `--stop-census` it instead runs only the adapter differential over the
corpus and prints why the tree scan left declarations unread: for every module
the first function, trait, implementation or global initializer it could not
read (where the tree path stops), and also every later one it tried. The table
ranks reasons by first stops, with one example `file:line` each. The reason is
the `StopReason` the tree parser's rollback carried; nothing is worked out from
text. The census checks nothing and is not part of the parity gate. A census over the
whole corpus also stores its per-module stops (see `--census-file`).

Targeted runs. Iterating on one stop reason should not cost a corpus run, so a
run can be narrowed to part of the corpus:

  * `--files PATH...` names tracked `.brp` files;
  * `--stop-reason LABEL` selects the modules whose first stop in the last full
    `--stop-census` had that label (the table's "First-stop modules").

Either narrows the parity run (token and verdict parity, then the adapter
differential with its tree-prefix and tree-module comparisons) or, with
`--stop-census`, the census; `--adapter-only` skips the token dumps, which a
tree-path change cannot affect. A targeted run compares only the selected
modules (the adapter differential still loads what they import), builds its
dumpers with `-O0` (the C compile is the larger cost at this size), skips the
root and graph checks and the corpus-wide allowance checks, and prints no
`BLORP_GATE_RESULT` line: it is not the gate, and the gate stays the full run.

The full census stores `stop-census.txt` under the system temporary directory,
in a directory named for this checkout (`--census-file` overrides it); a
targeted census never overwrites it.

Usage: scripts/compiler-new-parity [--keep DIR] [--compare OLD_DUMP NEW_DUMP]
                                   [--stop-census] [--census-file FILE]
                                   [--files PATH... | --stop-reason LABEL]
                                   [--adapter-only]
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
